  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Top Trumps. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Top Trumps is a trick-taking card game that involves tricks, trump, following suit. The game originated in Europe and has become popular worldwide.',
    objective: "Win all the cards by repeatedly winning rounds: in each round the active player chooses an attribute, everyone reveals that attribute's value from their top card, and the player with the highest (or best) value takes all the cards played that round and chooses the next attribute. The game ends when one player has collected the entire pack.",
    gameplay: '1. Setup: Deal all cards as equally as possible; each player holds their cards in a face-down stack, viewing only the top card. 2. Play: The starting player (normally left of dealer) chooses one attribute and reads its value from their top card; each other player reads the same attribute from their top card. The best value (usually highest; for some attributes like weight or time, lowest is better) wins the round. 3. Winner takes all the top cards from that round and places them at the bottom of their stack, then chooses the next attribute from their new top card. 4. Ties: If two or more players tie for best value, all played cards go to the center; the same player chooses again from the next card; the winner of that round also takes the center pile. If a player has no data for the chosen attribute, treat as a tie. 5. Elimination: Players drop out when they have no cards left. The winner is the player who collects the whole pack.',
    keyRules: [
      "Only the top card of each player's stack is in play each round",
      'The player who won the previous round chooses the attribute for the next round',
      'Best value wins the round (usually highest; some attributes use lowest-is-best)',
      'On a tie or no-data, cards go to the center; same player chooses again; next round winner takes center pile too',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'Minimum Players: 2\nMaximum Players: 6\nOptimal Players: 2–4\nPartnerships: No',
      deck: 'Type: Themed Top Trumps pack (typically 30, 32, 48 or 50 cards). Each card depicts one item (e.g. a car model, a dinosaur) and lists 5–8 attributes with numerical values (e.g. speed, length, power). Number of Decks: 1. Jokers: Not used.',
      equipment: 'One Top Trumps themed deck; table space. No score sheet required.',
      dealing: "All cards are dealt as equally as possible to the players. Each player holds their cards in a face-down stack so that only their top card is visible to them; opponents cannot see a player's cards. The starting player is normally the player to the dealer's left.",
    },
    turnFlow: '1. Setup: Deal all cards as equally as possible; each player holds their cards in a face-down stack, viewing only the top card. 2. Play: The starting player (normally left of dealer) chooses one attribute and reads its value from their top card; each other player reads the same attribute from their top card. The best value (usually highest; for some attributes like weight or time, lowest is better) wins the round. 3. Winner takes all the top cards from that round and places them at the bottom of their stack, then chooses the next attribute from their new top card. 4. Ties: If two or more players tie for best value, all played cards go to the center; the same player chooses again from the next card; the winner of that round also takes the center pile. If a player has no data for the chosen attribute, treat as a tie. 5. Elimination: Players drop out when they have no cards left. The winner is the player who collects the whole pack.',
